Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive summary report of the Firestore collections and schemas.

## Summary Report: Firestore Collections, Data Models, and Schema Definitions

Based on my comprehensive search of the beni-capital codebase, I've identified all the Firestore collections, their structures, and related data models. Here's the complete analysis:

### 1. TRANSACTIONS COLLECTION

**Location:** Root level collection: `db.collection('transactions')`

**TypeScript Interface:**
```typescript
interface Transaction {
  type: 'investment' | 'return';
  projectId: string;
  projectName: string;
  amount: number;
  accountName: string;
  date: number;              // Timestamp in milliseconds
  description: string;
  userId: string;            // CRITICAL: User who made the transaction
  userEmail: string;
}
```

**Files Using This Collection:**
- `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/lib/firebase/transaction-actions.ts` (Create & Query)
- `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/lib/firebase/investment-actions.ts` (Query/Read)
- `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/app/(dashboard)/dashboard/admin/projects/[id]/_fragments/AdminTransactions.tsx` (Display all transactions)
- `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/app/(dashboard)/dashboard/admin/projects/[id]/_fragments/Returns.tsx` (Display returns)
- `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/app/(dashboard)/dashboard/admin/projects/[id]/_fragments/AddReturnModal.tsx` (Create returns)

**Key Queries:**
- Get all transactions for a user: `where('userId', '==', userId)`
- Get transactions for a project: `where('projectId', '==', projectId)`
- Get only returns for a project: `where('projectId', '==', projectId) AND where('type', '==', 'return')`
- Get only investments for a project: `where('projectId', '==', projectId) AND where('type', '==', 'investment')`

---

### 2. PROJECTS COLLECTION

**Location:** Root level collection: `db.collection('projects')`

**TypeScript Interface:**
```typescript
interface Project {
  id: string;
  // Content properties
  name: string;
  madeBySubtitle: string;
  description: string;
  images: string[];
  videos: string[];
  heroImage: string;
  releaseDate: number;
  moneyRaised: number;
  createdAt: number;
  fundraisingEndDate: number;

  // Relationships & Complex Data
  overview: Overview;
  biography: string;
  creativeTeam: CreativeTeam[];
  cast: Cast[];
  investmentTerms: InvestmentTerms;
  financials: Financials;
  timeline: TimelineEvent[];
  monetizationAndDistribution: MonetizationAndDistribution;
  research: Research;
  updates: Update[];

  // Status & Metadata
  type: ProjectType;                    // 'theatre' | 'film' | 'tv' | 'music'
  status: ProjectStatus;                // 'closed' | 'in-production' | 'fundraising' | 'active' | 'fully-funded'
  comparableProjectIds: string[];       // Array of project IDs for comparison
}

// Nested Interfaces
interface Overview {
  description: string;
  categories: string[];
  directors: Director[];
  producers: Producer[];
  writers: Writer[];
}

interface Director {
  name: string;
  bio: string;
  image?: string;
}

interface Producer {
  name: string;
  bio: string;
  image?: string;
}

interface Writer {
  name: string;
  bio: string;
  image?: string;
}

interface InvestmentTerms {
  additionalData: { label: string; items: string[] | string; }[];
}

interface Financials {
  minInvestment: number;
  targetInvestment: number;
  totalBudget: number;
  projectedAudience?: number;
  projectedRevenue?: number;
  projectedReturn?: number;
  description?: string;
  budgetBreakdown?: BudgetBreakdown[];
  perks: Perk[];
  additionalData: { label: string; items: string | string[]; }[];
}

interface Perk {
  tier: 'Tier 1' | 'Tier 2' | 'Tier 3' | 'Tier 4' | 'Tier 5';
  title?: string;
  description?: string;
  options: string[];
}

interface BudgetBreakdown {
  label: string;
  amount: number;
}

interface CreativeTeam {
  name: string;
  role: string;
  bio: string;
  image?: string;
}

interface Cast {
  name: string;
  bio: string;
  image?: string;
}

interface TimelineEvent {
  date: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
}

interface MonetizationAndDistribution {
  additionalData: { label: string; items: string | string[]; }[];
}

interface Research {
  additionalData: { label: string; items: string | string[]; }[];
}

interface Update {
  title?: string;
  description: string;
  date: number;
}

type ProjectType = 'theatre' | 'film' | 'tv' | 'music';
type ProjectStatus = 'closed' | 'in-production' | 'fundraising' | 'active' | 'fully-funded';
```

**Files Using This Collection:**
- `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/lib/firebase/server-actions.ts` (CRUD operations)
- `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/lib/firebase/transaction-actions.ts` (Updates moneyRaised)

---

### 3. USERS COLLECTION

**Location:** Root level collection: `db.collection('users')`

**TypeScript Interfaces:**
```typescript
interface FirestoreUser {
  uid: string;
  email: string;
  createdAt: number;
  updatedAt: number;
  watchlist: string[];              // Array of project IDs
  displayName?: string;
  photoURL?: string;
  role?: 'admin' | null;            // CRITICAL: Admin role field
}

// Extended interface used in user-actions.ts
interface UserDocument {
  uid: string;
  email: string;
  displayName?: string;
  createdAt: number;
  updatedAt: number;
  photoURL?: string;
}
```

**Files Using This Collection:**
- `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/lib/firebase/user-actions.ts` (CRUD operations, watchlist management)
- `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/lib/firebase/server-actions.ts` (Admin role check: `isUserAdmin()`)

**Key Operations:**
- Check if user is admin: `userRef.data()?.role === 'admin'`
- Manage watchlist: `arrayUnion(projectId)` / `arrayRemove(projectId)`
- User document lifecycle: create on signup, update on profile changes

---

### 4. DOCUMENTS COLLECTION

**Location:** Root level collection: `db.collection('documents')`

**TypeScript Interface:**
```typescript
interface Document {
  id: string;
  documentUrl: string;
  projectId: string;
  projectName: string;
  date: number;              // Timestamp
  description: string;
}
```

**Status:** Currently using mock data in `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/app/(dashboard)/dashboard/my-investments/_fragments/my-documents/MyDocuments.tsx` - NOT YET integrated with Firestore.

**Files Using This Interface:**
- `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/types/document.ts` (Type definition)
- `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/app/(dashboard)/dashboard/my-investments/_fragments/my-documents/MyDocuments.tsx` (Display only - mock data)

---

### 5. RETURNS DATA (Stored in Transactions Collection)

**Note:** There is NO separate "returns" collection. Returns are stored as Transaction documents with `type: 'return'`.

**Return Transaction Structure (same as Transaction):**
```typescript
interface ReturnTransaction extends Transaction {
  type: 'return';
  projectId: string;
  projectName: string;
  amount: number;
  accountName: string;
  date: number;
  description: string;
  userId: string;            // Investor who receives the return
  userEmail: string;
}
```

**Files Managing Returns:**
- `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/lib/firebase/transaction-actions.ts` - `createReturnTransaction()`
- `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/app/(dashboard)/dashboard/admin/projects/[id]/_fragments/Returns.tsx` - Display returns for a project
- `/Users/stjepandzojic/projects/beni-capital/app/(dashboard)/dashboard/admin/projects/[id]/_fragments/AddReturnModal.tsx` - Add new return

---

### COLLECTION REFERENCES FOUND IN CODE

**All collection references discovered:**
```
db.collection('transactions')    - Root level
db.collection('projects')        - Root level
db.collection('users')           - Root level
db.collection('documents')       - Root level (type defined, not fully implemented in Firestore yet)
```

---

### SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS FOR FIRESTORE RULES

**Key Fields for Authorization:**
1. **`userId`** in transactions - Used to determine if a user can read their own transactions
2. **`role`** in users - Used to determine admin access (value: 'admin' or null)
3. **`projectId`** in transactions/documents - Used to scope access to project-related data

**Current Security Gaps (based on code analysis):**
- No existing Firestore rules file found in the project
- `isUserAdmin()` function exists in server-actions.ts but needs to be enforced at the database level
- Transaction creation doesn't validate user ownership
- No read restrictions on transactions (anyone could potentially read all transactions)
- No document-level security on projects or documents collections

**Recommended Rule Scopes:**
- Transactions: Should be readable only by the user who created them (userId check) or admins
- Projects: Should be publicly readable for unauthenticated browsing, but some fields might be admin-only
- Users: Should be private (only own document readable), except admin data for admins
- Documents: Should be readable only by the user or admins

---

